  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 310 AM EDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nHigh pressure will slowly build in over the course of the long term. \nThis will continue to decrease chances gradually of afternoon \nthunderstorms while slowly increasing afternoon high temps and with \nit heat indices. Temps will return to the mid 90s by the middle of \nthe week with widespread triple digit heat index values along and \nsouth of I-85. A heat advisory may be needed for the southern \nportions of the CWA as early as Monday. \n\nOvernight lows will also be on the rise with the return of the mid \n70s to much of the area. This doesn't do much in providing relief \nfrom the daytime heat; especially for vulnerable populations. Look \nafter each other, and keep an eye on pets and kids. Stay hydrated if \nyou plan to spend time outside.\n\nThunderstorm chances during the afternoon will be down to less than \n10% for much of the area through the week. As a result, the chances \nof cooling off with an afternoon thunderstorm decrease with it. \nSummer is still here and it's planning to stick around for a\nwhile.",
